This commit message itself trips its own detector. It quotes "utilize,"
which costs the flat +8 penalty, so it scores 3.3 total while the prose
alone scores -4.7. Step 5 treats this as the exception it is built to
catch, and the new output shows it clearly instead of leaving a bare
3.3 unexplained.

I left the score limits (5 and 10) unchanged. They were set using
messages with no stock-phrase hits, so for an honest draft the total
and the prose-only score are the same number. Changing the limits now
would undo the calibration recorded in commit e39c59c.

I also considered removing the phrase penalty from the total entirely.
Tested against the three example messages in SLOP_VARIANTS, they score
24.0, 9.6, and 5.8 without it. The 5.8 score falls inside the range of
real commit messages, meaning the detector would miss the case it was
built to catch.
